"The setup package is ready: **Shelfmate**, using the existing JavaScript/Node.js stack, with **5 phases and 10 tickets**. The first version covers the teacher’s full find → lend → return → overdue workflow, with data preserved across restarts.\n\nProposed assumptions: keep the API-only interface, run locally for one teacher, treat each book record as one physical copy, and let the teacher enter the due date. An active loan becomes overdue the day after that date. Returning a book removes the pupil label from current application data; backup retention is documented separately.\n\nPhases are milestones; tickets are demonstrable pieces of work. The labels below are proposal references—Storybloq assigns IDs during creation.\n\n| Milestone | Ticket | Purpose | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Setup | Default phase | Storybloq configuration and context | — |\n| Existing catalogue | B1 Catalogue baseline | Record verified list/add functionality as complete | — |\n| Reliable catalogue | F1 Safe API requests | Validate input, handle errors, bound requests, restrict access to localhost | — |\n| Reliable catalogue | F2 Persistent storage | Save books and stable IDs; handle corruption, concurrent writes, and crash recovery | F1 |\n| Reliable catalogue | F3 Search | Find copies by title or author | F1 |\n| Reliable catalogue | C1 Teacher checkpoint | Review sample add/search/restart workflow and book-copy model | F2, F3 |\n| Circulation | F4 Lending | Record pupil and due date; prevent double lending; persist loans | C1 |\n| Circulation | F5 Returns | Make books available again; safely handle repeated returns | F4 |\n| Circulation | F6 Overdue list | Show active overdue loans with book, pupil, and due date | F4 |\n| First-version acceptance | V1 Journey verification | Test actual process restarts through the full workflow; update README and recovery instructions | F5, F6 |\n| First-version acceptance | C2 Teacher acceptance | Demonstrate every agreed first-version outcome | V1 |\n\nAll requested outcomes are covered. A browser interface, hosting, notifications, and loan history remain outside this version. Checkpoints are ordinary tickets; Storybloq does not technically enforce owner approval.\n\nIndependent review approved the plan with two corrections, now incorporated: distinguish failed writes from ambiguous failures after a file replacement, and test safe lock recovery after crashes. No review findings remain unresolved.\n\nApproval covers:\n\n- `.story/` configuration, roadmap, tickets, baseline snapshot, setup note, and initial handover.\n- `AGENTS.md`, `RULES.md`, and the standard `REVIEW.md` contract.\n- Git initialization and ignores for Storybloq runtime files and local pupil data.\n- **Full pipeline** quality settings because lending involves business rules and durable state:\n\n| Stage | Configuration |\n|---|---|\n| Write tests / Test | `npm test` — established |\n| Build | Disabled; no build script |\n| Verify | `npm start`, checking `http://localhost:3000/books` — established |\n\nNo tests, server, or installation commands were run, and no project files have changed.\n\nWould you like to **approve setup**, adjust the plan, or inspect ticket/file details?\n\nThe [setup flow](/private/tmp/cc-cpm-w4-t525/onboarding-eval-OocqOy/home/.agents/skills/story/setup-flow.md) explicitly requires this final approval: “nothing in 1e runs until the user explicitly chooses ‘Approve setup’.” Approval authorizes creating the package above."
